@startuml token_refresh_sequence

!theme plain

title Token Refresh Flow

autonumber

skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFFFBD
}

actor "User Agent\n(Browser)" as UA
participant "Frontend Portal" as PORTAL
participant "Flexibility\nInformation System (FIS)\nAuth API" as AUTH
database "Database\nauth.session\nauth.token" as DB

note over PORTAL
    The access token (JWT) has expired
    or is about to expire.
    Only one refresh runs at a time.
end note

PORTAL -> AUTH: POST /auth/v1/refresh\n<:cookie:> __Host-flex_session (session token)\n<:cookie:> __Host-flex_access (possibly expired JWT)

note over AUTH
    Verify the access token:
    signature, issuer, audience and type.
    The expiry is ignored.
end note

alt access token is invalid
    AUTH --> PORTAL: HTTP 401\nUnset <:cookie:> __Host-flex_session\nUnset <:cookie:> __Host-flex_access
    PORTAL -> UA: Go to /#/login
end

AUTH -> DB: Look up hash of session token\nand its session
DB --> AUTH

alt session token is unknown or expired,\nor entity does not match the access token
    AUTH --> PORTAL: HTTP 401\nUnset <:cookie:> __Host-flex_session\nUnset <:cookie:> __Host-flex_access
    PORTAL -> UA: Go to /#/login
else session token was used a few seconds ago
    note over AUTH
        Probably a concurrent refresh.
        Nothing is changed.
    end note
    AUTH --> PORTAL: HTTP 409
    note over PORTAL
        Retry with the cookies
        set by the other refresh.
    end note
else session token was used earlier
    note over AUTH
        Outdated but valid token:
        it was probably copied.
    end note
    AUTH -> DB: Revoke the session
    AUTH --> PORTAL: HTTP 401\nUnset <:cookie:> __Host-flex_session\nUnset <:cookie:> __Host-flex_access
    PORTAL -> UA: Go to /#/login
else session token is valid
    AUTH -> DB: Mark token as used and insert a\nnew token in the session (same expires_at)
    DB --> AUTH
    note over AUTH
        Issue a new access token with the same party and scope.
        Its lifetime is the remaining session lifetime.
    end note
    AUTH --> PORTAL: HTTP 200\nSet <:cookie:> __Host-flex_session (new)\nSet <:cookie:> __Host-flex_access (new)
    note over PORTAL
        The original request
        can now be retried.
    end note
end

|||
@enduml
